      <p>Applying for a banking or SSC exam instead? See the <a href="/blog/ssc-cgl-photo-signature-upload-guide">SSC CGL upload guide</a>, the <a href="/blog/ibps-po-photo-signature-thumb-declaration">IBPS PO upload guide</a>, or the <a href="/blog/compress-images-indian-government-forms">full spec reference for SSC, IBPS, UPSC, PAN, and Aadhaar</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="key-takeaways">Key Takeaways</h2>

      <ol>
        <li><strong>Dimensions and aspect ratio matter as much as file size</strong> — GATE enforces both, and a correctly-sized-in-KB file can still fail on shape.</li>
        <li><strong>NEET and JEE Main share the same photo/signature dimensions</strong> (3.5&times;4.5 cm / 3.5&times;1.5 cm) but different KB ranges — don't assume they're identical.</li>
        <li><strong>JEE Main's 2026 KB limits changed mid-cycle</strong> — always check the current bulletin, not a cached guide.</li>
        <li><strong>RRB has no single national spec</strong> — confirm against the specific CEN notification for your recruitment before uploading.</li>
        <li><strong>Resize first, then compress</strong> — compressing an unresized photo just produces a smaller version of a file that was already the wrong shape.</li>
      </ol>

